course: dictionary
lesson: 6943
title: Painless and its clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pain is the hurt you feel in your body. The ending -less means without, so painless means without any pain. Careless means without care, and hopeless means without hope.
explain: «Sealants and fluoride varnish are quick, painless coatings that help protect the back teeth from decay.» The clues are quick and protect. A painless coating does not hurt, and it helps keep the teeth healthy.
explain: Painless can also mean easy and not unpleasant. «The check-up was painless» means it did not hurt and it went smoothly. Ask yourself: does the sentence still make sense if I put in "did not hurt"?
fact: Painless means not causing any pain.
fact: Painless can also mean easy and not unpleasant, as in «a painless way to learn spelling».
fact: The adverb is «painlessly», which means in a way that does not cause pain.
fact: The ending -less means without, so painless means without pain.
fact: A «painless injection» is one that does not hurt when the needle goes in.
exercise: «Sealants are quick, painless coatings for the back teeth.» What does painless mean here? | Very bright and shiny | Costing a lot of money | Very large and heavy | *Not causing any pain
exercise: Ella says the test was painless. What does she mean? | The test was held in a big hall | The test was painful and very slow | *The test was easy and not unpleasant | The test was lost in the post
exercise: Which word is the adverb form of painless? | pain | *painlessly | painless | painful
test: «The injection was painless, so Sam did not even wince.» What does painless mean in this sentence? | Very long | Very cold | Brightly coloured | *Did not hurt
test: Which word means the same as "without pain"? | *painless | hopeful | careless | painful
exam: «The vaccine was quick and painless, and the nurse said I was brave.» What does painless suggest? | It was something you had to pay for | It was loud and sudden | *It did not hurt, and it was easy | It was a very long wait
